Another way to show it

The kableExtra package has many features for making HTML-format tables.
You could try making a table if you choose to work on Exercise 05.


my_stats_df |&gt;
  kableExtra::kable() |&gt;
  kableExtra::kable_classic()

Clean data

pa_higher_ed_trimmed &lt;- pa_higher_ed |&gt;
  rename(lon = Longitude,
         lat = Latitude) |&gt;
  select(Sector, College, Type, County, lon, lat) |&gt;
  filter(!is.na(lat) &
         !is.na(lon))

Higher ed data

Summarize the number of institutions per county


pa_higher_ed_counties &lt;- pa_higher_ed_trimmed |&gt;
  group_by(County) |&gt;
  summarize(n_institutions = n())

Higher ed data

pa_higher_ed_counties |&gt;
  kableExtra::kable() |&gt;
  kableExtra::kable_material()

